Log every shared_region_map_and_slide_2_np call and result to COM5.

A stalled boot shows launchd reaching dyld, getting
"result from check_np(): -1, errno 12" (the documented normal
"shared region is empty" response, also present in every successful
boot), and then never logging "dyld cache mapped system-wide".

The syscall that would establish the mapping is
shared_region_map_and_slide_2_np() (536). Its tracing is behind
SHARED_REGION_TRACE_DEBUG/_ERROR, which the release kernel does not
emit, so the log cannot distinguish "never called" from "called and
failed". This prints once on entry and once on exit, including the
failure return code. Side-effect free: printf only, no state.
diff --git a/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c b/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c
index 64d187a..d4fa5dc 100644
--- a/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c
+++ b/bsd/vm/vm_unix.c
@@ -2186,6 +2186,14 @@ shared_region_map_and_slide_2_np(
 	struct shared_file_mapping_slide_np *mappings = NULL;
 	kern_return_t                 kr = KERN_SUCCESS;
 
+#if defined(__arm64__)
+	/* TB710FU: unconditional trace. The release kernel does not emit
+	 * SHARED_REGION_TRACE_*, so a stalled boot cannot otherwise tell
+	 * "dyld never called map_and_slide" from "it was called and failed". */
+	printf("TB710FU SRMAP[%d]: enter files=%u mappings=%u\n",
+	    proc_getpid(p), uap->files_count, uap->mappings_count);
+#endif
+
 	files_count = uap->files_count;
 	mappings_count = uap->mappings_count;
 
@@ -2345,6 +2353,12 @@ done:
 		proc_getpid(p), p->p_comm,
 		(uint64_t)uap->mappings_u, kr));
 
+#if defined(__arm64__)
+	/* TB710FU: one line per call, covering every failure path above. */
+	printf("TB710FU SRMAP[%d]: exit kr=0x%x files=%u mappings=%u\n",
+	    proc_getpid(p), kr, files_count, mappings_count);
+#endif
+
 	return kr;
 }
 
